# Timer and score. PDF page 5, printed page 3, block S.
# Written like a MAME netlist: chips by location, then each wire as the pins it joins.
# tools/generate_netlist.py names the Verilog wires from the pins: docs/NET_NAMES.md.
# OPEN identifies a visibly unconnected input; it is not a missed wire.
chip L12 74151
chip M12 74151
chip N12 74151
chip P12 74151
chip P14 7432
chip N14 7420
chip P13 74157
# SPCA fans down to P14.10 and M15.9; 5SPCL crosses it without a dot
# and continues to M14.11. These are separate vertical wires on sheet 3.
chip M15 7400
chip M14 7410
prom N13 82S123 33
chip M13 74151
chip L13 74112
chip M16 7404
# Fixed 2026-11-05: pin 2 is the raw 2-minute line, ahead of inverter M16. Death Race 14V agrees.
# Fixed 2026-11-05: 4=SG20, 5=5SG20, 6=S999 on this drawing; Death Race 14U agrees.
chip N16 74161
chip K13 7408
chip P16 74192
chip P15 74192
chip N15 7402
chip G13 7402
chip M11 74192
chip L11 74192
chip P11 74192
chip N11 74192

# Wires: drawing label, then every pin it joins on this sheet. BOARD marks a
# wire that rtl/deathrac_board.v drives or reads. GND/VCC are tied pins, OPEN a
# visibly floating input, NC a drawn output stub that goes nowhere.
net OPEN L12.1 L12.12 M12.1 M12.12 N12.1 N12.12 P12.1 P12.12
net STC7 L12.2 P15.7 N15.8 BOARD
net SLC3 L12.3 M11.7
net SLC7 L12.4 L11.7
net SCS3 L12.5 P13.1 P14.9
net NC L12.6 M12.6 N12.6 P12.6 L13.9 N16.11 N16.12 N16.13 N16.14 P15.13 P15.12 L11.13 L11.12 N11.13 N11.12
net GND L12.7 M12.7 N12.7 P12.7 P13.15 N13.15 P16.14 P16.1 P16.10 P15.14 P15.1 P15.10 M11.15 M11.1 M11.10 M11.9 L11.15 L11.1 L11.10 L11.9 P11.15 P11.1 P11.10 P11.9 N11.15 N11.1 N11.10 N11.9
net TEC8 L12.9 M12.9 N12.9 P12.9 N14.4
net TSS1 L12.10 M12.10 N12.10 P12.10 P14.2 M15.5
net TSS0 L12.11 M12.11 N12.11 P12.11 P14.1 M15.4
net SRC3 L12.13 P11.7
net SRC7 L12.14 N11.7
net STC3 L12.15 P16.7 N15.6 BOARD
net STC6 M12.2 P15.6 N15.9 BOARD
net SLC2 M12.3 M11.6
net SLC6 M12.4 L11.6
net SCS2 M12.5 P13.2
net SRC2 M12.13 P11.6
net SRC6 M12.14 N11.6
